GPPS Policy Data -- Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) Report

1. Executive Summary

An exploratory analysis was performed on the GPPS policy data across
Global and multiple market/country-level policy tables, with particular
focus on:

Policy population and market coverage

Policy/object relationships (objRel)

Relationship types (plcyObjTypeCde)

Control, policy and regulatory relationships

Control identifiers (cntId) and identifier formats

Segment-level information (sgmntTypeCde)

Policy and segment text completeness

Potentially inactive/retired policies

Cross-market consistency of the GPPS data model

The EDA indicates that the GPPS data is not structurally uniform
across Global and all markets. There are meaningful differences in
policy volumes, relationship availability, relationship types,
identifier usage and text completeness.

The most significant finding is that regulatory relationships
(plcyObjTypeCde = 'REG') appear to be concentrated in the US data,
while the other observed markets and Global predominantly show CNTRL
and/or PLCY relationships. This needs confirmation from the Policies
team before any downstream logic treats the absence of REG
relationships as a genuine business condition.

Similarly, Global appears to use sgmntTypeCde more directly for
control/segment classification, while market-level records appear to
rely more heavily on objRel. This may represent an intentional
difference in the GPPS data model, but it should be confirmed.

The EDA also identified several data-quality and completeness questions,
including very small policy populations in certain markets, extremely
short text values in some markets, missing top-level policy text for at
least one Australian record, and records that appear to be retired or
inactive.

2. Scope of Analysis

The analysis covered the following broad areas:

Area                                Objective

Policy population                   Understand the number of policies
available by market

objRel                            Understand relationships between
policies/objects

plcyObjTypeCde                    Identify control, policy and
regulatory relationships

cntId                             Assess identifier patterns and
completeness

sgmntTypeCde                      Understand segment classification
and population

